-(`MISSING` and `MALFORMED` sit outside this derivation — they are registration and contract faults.) Automatic selection runs READY sets in scheduler order and passes over DONE, DEFERRED, and AWAITING-APPROVAL sets; only when no READY set exists may a no-argument implement select a single unambiguous Human-blocked Task set for attended help, and only when the block is an open HITL task rather than an unresolved AFK dependency. Multiple Human-blocked Task sets are ambiguous and require an explicit target. Draining stops when its selected set reaches DONE, FAILED, BLOCKED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, VERIFY-FAILED, or DEFERRED, or when an **Agent quota pause** interrupts draining without changing task status. At a BLOCKED HITL gate, interactive runs show a **HITL gate prompt** while non-interactive runs and `--yes` preserve stop-and-advice output and never auto-start attended assistance.
+(`MISSING` and `MALFORMED` sit outside this derivation — they are registration and contract faults. `EXPLORE-FAILED` is layered on top of it: a READY set that declared the **Explore directive**, has no **Exploration report**, and has a **Captured run** of phase `explore` reads EXPLORE-FAILED instead, so nothing re-picks it — see **Explore phase**.) Automatic selection runs READY sets in scheduler order and passes over DONE, DEFERRED, and AWAITING-APPROVAL sets; only when no READY set exists may a no-argument implement select a single unambiguous Human-blocked Task set for attended help, and only when the block is an open HITL task rather than an unresolved AFK dependency. Multiple Human-blocked Task sets are ambiguous and require an explicit target. Draining stops when its selected set reaches DONE, FAILED, BLOCKED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, VERIFY-FAILED, EXPLORE-FAILED, or DEFERRED, or when an **Agent quota pause** interrupts draining without changing task status. At a BLOCKED HITL gate, interactive runs show a **HITL gate prompt** while non-interactive runs and `--yes` preserve stop-and-advice output and never auto-start attended assistance.
 
 **Tasks readiness**:
 The **Doctor status** of the `pop tasks` command family. Because the tasks feature is aimed at Git projects and its central workflow is agent execution from a **Runtime path**, Doctor reports `pop tasks` as Blocked when no Git runtime checkout can be resolved, even if read-only status rendering could still inspect local artifacts.
@@ -762,6 +762,26 @@ _Avoid_: verify result, verification status
 The **Drain** step, formerly Code review, that enforces the resolved `refine` **Convention kind** on a **Task set**'s accumulated changeset: a fresh **Refiner** researches the changeset, fixes in place what the convention licenses, and writes the **Refine report** of what it fixed and the smells it left. It runs at AFK quiescence *before* the verify phase, so its edits are judged by the same **Agent verification** pass as the work they refine — reversing the after-verify placement, which was derived from the step moving nothing. Set-scoped, gated by `[work.refine].enabled` (off by default); it reaches no verdict and spawns no tasks — its outputs are the **Refine commit** and the report. Automatic Refine skips a **Human completion** (the drain never edits code a human declared done); `pop tasks refine` runs a full pass by hand on any set with a done AFK task and a non-empty commit range, including a human-completed or DONE one — the human re-opening the question.
 _Avoid_: Code review, code quality check, review step, polish, lint step, QA
 
+**Explore phase**:
+The **Drain** step that writes a **Task set**'s **Exploration report** before its first task runs (ADR-0262). It runs at the head of a drain, before task selection, for a set that carries the **Explore directive** and has no report; a set with a report reuses it and spends nothing, and nothing compares the report's recorded tree to the checkout — absent means write, present means reuse. Gated by `[work.explore].enabled`, which defaults *on*: the first agent phase that runs unasked, safe because only the set's own directive triggers it. It is also the one agent phase that gates: a pass that cannot write the report within the standard per-phase retry cap parks the set at EXPLORE-FAILED — VERIFY-FAILED's sibling, not BLOCKED, which keeps meaning a human owes a decision — and appends one set-level **Progress record** naming the phase and the reason. The park is derived from the **Captured run** of phase `explore` plus the absent report, with no store column. Three ways out: `pop tasks explore <set>` by hand, `pop tasks implement <set> --skip-explore` to drain once unexplored, or `"explore": false`. It declines a **Human completion**, and `pop tasks explore` runs on any set whatever its directive says, overwriting a report already there.
+_Avoid_: survey, discovery step, pre-flight, context pass
+
+**Explore directive**:
+The set-level `"explore": true` manifest key: the set's author declaring that two or more AFK tasks touch the same seam and a later one depends on how an earlier one shapes it. Opt-*in* — absent or false means the set never explores — where the `verify` and `refine` keys are opt-out. It sits outside the **Agent directive** family, whose members steer how a phase runs and never opt a set in; the `"explorer"` object beside it is that family's member for the **Explore phase**. Never set for a set's size or an unfamiliar area.
+_Avoid_: explore flag, interrelated flag
+
+**Exploration report**:
+The code as found in the area a **Task set**'s tasks touch, at `exploration.md` flat in the set directory, written by the **Explore phase**'s **Explorer**: where things live, which seam owns what, which invariants hold, the test shape, which files to read in ranges — every claim naming a path or a symbol, about a page, stating the tree it describes as prose and in its header. A **Task artifact** ordered spec → exploration → progress (what was decided, what exists, what happened), exempt from the orphan-markdown check like `spec.md`. Every implement attempt on the set is handed its path, never its body, with one correction duty: a builder may fix a line its own attempt falsified and change nothing else. It carries no prior-art section. An **Explore mark** beside the status says whether a declared set got one.
+_Avoid_: map, context file, survey, notes
+
+**Explore mark**:
+Whether a **Task set** that carries the **Explore directive** has its **Exploration report**: explored, or unexplored with its reason — not yet run, or the pass failed — as detail beside the mark rather than a value inside it. A set that never declared exploration carries none. Resolved once on the read side (`ResolveExploreMark`) and rendered by the dashboard row and detail view, `pop work status`, `pop tasks status` and the sign-off gate.
+_Avoid_: explore status, exploration badge
+
+**Explorer**:
+The agent that performs the **Explore phase**, fresh and chosen from `[work.explore]` / the set's `"explorer"` object / CLI flags. The one role spawned under the **Read-only agent posture**: its reply is the whole report, which pop writes.
+_Avoid_: scout, mapper
+
 **Refiner**:
 Formerly the Reviewer. The agent that performs **Refine**, running in a fresh context and chosen independently of the implementing agents so it does not refine its own work — the **Verifier**'s independence rule, for the same reason. Its prompt is pop's own end to end (ADR-0246, ADR-0247): pop's **Role preamble**, the **Implementation convention** as a labelled block, any **Convention overlay** on the procedure, and pop's **Response contract**, plus the previous **Refine report** where one exists. The convention states the standard; the licence is pop's and the convention cannot widen it — fix what the pass can undo, and show the search that licensed it (ADR-0248); anything it cannot prove reversible stays a finding in the report. It reads the changed files itself — the commit range and the **Work diff view** are orientation only. No longer spawned under a **Read-only agent posture**, and it never commits: the runner captures its edits as the **Refine commit**.
 _Avoid_: Reviewer, polisher, fixer, critic, linter
